{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0116iKPHM8pptDWTr9mWir1q","type":"tool_result","content":"=== c_src unmodified (mtimes = original 04:15) ===\n2026-08-20 04:15  c_src/CMakeLists.txt\n2026-08-20 04:15  c_src/license.txt\n2026-08-20 04:15  c_src/include/lib.h\n2026-08-20 04:15  c_src/src/lib.c\n=== deliverables in cwd ===\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 195 Aug 20 04:16 Cargo.toml\n\nsrc/:\ntotal 40\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon    20 Aug 20 04:18 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 6 scheschb amazon 16384 Aug 20 04:23 ..\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 20661 Aug 20 04:18 lib.rs\n=== Cargo.toml ===\n[lib]\nname = \"translated_rust\"\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f37ce8b-4a53-488a-949a-949c7602f74e","uuid":"09c993ac-767b-4d44-b46c-ec70a72ab969","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:23:07.413Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== c_src unmodified (mtimes = original 04:15) ===\n2026-08-20 04:15  c_src/CMakeLists.txt\n2026-08-20 04:15  c_src/license.txt\n2026-08-20 04:15  c_src/include/lib.h\n2026-08-20 04:15  c_src/src/lib.c\n=== deliverables in cwd ===\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 195 Aug 20 04:16 Cargo.toml\n\nsrc/:\ntotal 40\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 scheschb amazon    20 Aug 20 04:18 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 6 scheschb amazon 16384 Aug 20 04:23 ..\n-rw-r--r--. 1 scheschb amazon 20661 Aug 20 04:18 lib.rs\n=== Cargo.toml ===\n[lib]\nname = \"translated_rust\"\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uvy7oclumqqyki5kvb7kbnl4vkpkyxeytpb6kbwyka33mg6tqwjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the C library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single-TU library (`src/lib.c`, 402 lines) — a subset of the `cute_c2` 2D collision-detection routines, plus the public `poly_ray` entry point declared in `include/lib.h`. No namespace-renaming macros are present, so linker symbols equal source names.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `src/lib.rs` — 797 lines, 28 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"` functions\n\n## Symbol-parity gate: PASSED\n\n`nm -D` diff between the C `.so` (built via its own CMakeLists) and the Rust `.so` is **empty** — all 28 exports match:\n\n```\nc2V c2Dot c2Len c2Add c2Sub c2Mulvs c2Div c2Norm c2Minv c2Maxv c2Skew c2Absv\nc2CCW90 c2MulmvT c2RotIdentity c2xIdentity c2Mulrv c2MulrvT c2MulxvT\nc2AABBtoAABB c2AABBtoPoint c2CircleToPoint\nc2RaytoCircle c2RaytoAABB c2RaytoCapsule c2RaytoPoly c2CastRay poly_ray\n```\n\nThe Rust `.so` exports *no* extra symbols either. The two `static inline` helpers (`c2SignedDistPointToPlane_OneDimensional`, `c2RayToPlane_OneDimensional`) are correctly kept private, matching C.\n\n## Byte-identical output: verified by differential harness\n\nI built a `dlopen`-based harness that loads both `.so`s side-by-side and `memcmp`s raw bit patterns of every function's return value *and* its `c2Raycast` out-param (with the out-buffer pre-poisoned to `0x5A` so \"didn't write\" is also compared).\n\n**11,400,005 bit-exact comparisons × 5 C optimization levels (-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os) → 0 mismatches**, over inputs including ±0.0, ±inf, denormals, mixed magnitudes, all four `C2_TYPE` tags plus an invalid tag, null and non-null `c2x*`, and `c2Poly.count` from 0–8.\n\n`poly_ray()` returns `0` and leaves both out-params untouched in C and Rust identically.\n\nOne nuance worth flagging: with **NaN** inputs there are ~53k lane differences — but these are pure NaN-payload propagation, and **the C library does not reproduce them stably against itself** (C `-O0` vs C `-O2` differ in 102,221 lanes, in the exact same function categories). With a tolerance that only forgives lanes where *both* sides are NaN, Rust matches all five C builds with 0 failures. So this is inherent C/hardware nondeterminism, not a translation defect.\n\n## Fidelity details preserved\n\n- The C source expands `c2Abs`/`c2Min`/`c2Max` into ternaries (`a < 0 ? -a : a`). I replicated the conditional form via private `c_abs`/`c_min`/`c_max` rather than `f32::abs`/`min`/`max`, which differ for NaN and signed zero.\n- `int index = ~0` and the `index != ~0` sentinel comparison kept as `-1`.\n- `c2RaytoPoly` uses raw pointer offsets for `verts[i]`/`norms[i]`, so a `count > 8` reads past the array exactly as C does instead of panicking.\n- `c2RaytoCapsule`'s dead `M`/`cap_n`/`yAd` computations, the redundant `capsule_a`/`capsule_b` vs `Ca`/`Cb` duplication, and the unconditional `out->n`/`out->t` pre-write before the early returns are all retained.\n- Error-check and early-return ordering is unchanged throughout; no bugs were \"fixed.\""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":725,"cache_read_input_tokens":63307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":725,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f37ce8b-4a53-488a-949a-949c7602f74e","uuid":"d564cce3-51df-4512-b904-a8bd677f99ea","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:23:27.372Z"}
